// Engine test (session 3): every game system in one short chapter. Not part of the story.
// Developer books may print raw numbers; story chapters use voice() instead.
@chapter etc1
@title Engine Test: Systems
@book engine-test-c
@version 1

# start
## Day and night
$ wealth = 500
$ do phase("day")
Day phase with {actions_left()} actions. Collis here is {collis()}.
* Invest in wine and oil ?if can_invest("rome.wine")
  $ do invest("rome.wine")
  $ do act()
  Collis owns the wine trade at level {venture_level("rome.wine")}.
* Rebuild the village houses ?if can_build("rebuilt_houses")
  $ do build("rebuilt_houses")
  $ do act()
  Collesanto rebuilt: {built("rebuilt_houses")}.
:day_done
$ do act(1, true)
Midday cost hunger. {actions_left()} action(s) left. In phase: {in_phase()}.
---
-> night

# night
$ do phase("night", 2)
$ do feed("animal")
Fed on animal blood ({fed("animal")} time). Hunger is now {hunger}.
$ do choose_path("coven")
$ do sire("et_fledgling", "scout", true)
Sired: {in_circle("et_fledgling")}, power {member_power("et_fledgling")}, daywalker {daywalker("et_fledgling")}.
$ do keeper("et_keeper", "steward")
$ do send("et_fledgling", "scout", 1)
On a mission: {on_mission("et_fledgling")}. Coven {coven_size()}, circle {circle_size()}.
$ do meet("et_love")
$ do romance("et_love")
Romance: {romance_status("et_love")}, partner {partner()}.
$ do obtain("gladius")
Items: {item_count()}.
$ do awaken("general", "bloodline")
The General is {original("general")}, woken by {original("general", "by")}. Awake: {awake_count()}.
---
-> fight

# fight
$ do fight("human", 3)
:exchange
* Feint
  $ do strike("cunning")
* Overpower
  $ do strike("brutal")
?if not fight_over()
  Exchange: {last_strike()}.
  -> :exchange
?end
The fight ended: {fight_result()}.
---
-> rest

# rest
$ do rest()
Rested. Income {rested("income")}, missions back {rested("missions")}.
Mission report: {mission("et_fledgling")}.
$ do debrief("et_fledgling")
$ do romance_end("et_love", "parted")
The romance ended: {romance_ending("et_love")}.
---
=> endbook
